 jet of C–D gas die and external wall of melt delivery nozzle. This phenomenon was not observed in the case of flow separation phenomenon in which the gas boundary layer separation is highly related to the gas travel distance or melt delivery tip length where the greater given distance to the boundary layer flow distance, the greater flow separation that occurs [15]. So decreasing the distance between the exit of the gas jet and the external wall of the melt delivery nozzle has been proposed by authors as a means of mitigating the back-streaming phenomenon. In order to investigate the effect of this separation on the
